'''Misha Sharuk''' was a [[human]] [[Jedi Knight]]<ref name="TVG" /> that lived during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=day-trivia-gallery-the-acolyte|text="Day" Trivia Gallery &#124; The Acolyte}} {{C|Slide 5}}</ref> In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> Sharuk was briefed by [[Jedi Knight]] [[Yord Fandar]] on a [[Mission to Khofar|mission]] to [[Khofar]] to locate secluded [[Jedi Master]] [[Kelnacca]].<ref name="Day" />

Sharuk accompanied a team led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]] through the forests of Khofar in search of Kelnacca. As night began to fall, the team eventually reached [[Kelnacca's shelter]] and demanded the surrender of anyone inside. Unbeknownst to them, a mysterious [[The Stranger|stranger]] approached them from behind. Sharuk ignited her [[lightsaber]]s in response to the Stranger drawing his [[The Stranger's lightsaber|blade]]. Charging him, Sharuk was flung back by a powerful [[Force push]]. In the ensuing battle, Sharuk's blade was shorted-out by the Stranger's [[cortosis gauntlet]]. then shortly being saved by Yord Fandar, After regaining the use of her lightsaber, she attempted to engage the Stranger, but Sharuk was promptly impaled through the chest by the Stranger who then [[Telekinesis|pulled]] [[Inro Jadrel]] into his still ignited blade, then beheading both her and Jadrel, killing them both instantly.<ref name="Night">{{Acolyte|Night}}</ref>

{{Char-stub}}

==Equipment==
Misha Sharuk wore brown [[Jedi apparel]] with gold accents, and wielded a [[lightsaber]] with a [[Color|blue]] blade.<ref name="Day" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:HarukaOshimaCool.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Haruka Oshima portrayed Misha Sharuk in ''Star Wars: The Acolyte'']]
The Jedi, albeit unidentified, first appeared in "[[Day (episode)|Day]],"<ref name="Day" /> the fourth episode of the live-action series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', which premiered [[June 18]], [[2024]].<ref name="EPG">{{SW|url=series/the-acolyte/season-1-episode-4-day-episode-guide|text="Day" Episode Guide &#124; The Acolyte}}</ref> She was played by stunt performer, [[Haruka Oshima]].<ref name="Tweet">{{Twitter|username=_harururu_|url=status/1803373527044665683|name=[[Haruka Oshima]]|date=2024-06-19|quote=アコライト4話！遂に大島ジェダイ出たそうです！自分のSW知識はファンの方の足元にも及ばないので人伝てではあるのですが、どうやら史上初の日本人ジェダイらしい…？との事で…！感謝感激雨あられ、今まで頑張って来てよかった…！まさか自分がジェダイになれる日が来るとは…😭#アコライト #大島遥|archivedate=20240627142744}}</ref> According to her, the Jedi's name on the call sheet was KNIGHT2.<ref name="Tweet2">{{Twitter|username=_harururu_|url=status/1803374578032418849|name=[[Haruka Oshima]]|date=2024-06-19|quote=あークレジットだとジェダイナイトって書いて貰えなかったか…残念…コールシートには書いてあるんだけどな…KNIGHT2って…残念|archiveurl=https://archive.md/ET1fV}}</ref> She was later identified as Misha Sharuk in the reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]''.<ref name="TVG" />

